Subject: [PATCH] sysv: wait for the GTX HCI UART and system bus at boot

OpenATV launches runlevel 3 services in parallel. On a GTX the UniSoc
firmware registers hci0 after the BlueZ startup script has already run.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [GTX-specific parallel SysV startup]

--- a/bluetooth
+++ b/bluetooth
@@ -29,6 +29,13 @@
 		echo "disabled (see /etc/default/bluetooth)."
 		exit 0
 	fi
+	# Runlevel 3 starts D-Bus and gtx-wireless concurrently with bluetoothd.
+	for attempt in $(seq 1 15); do
+		if [ -d /sys/class/bluetooth/hci0 ] && [ -S /run/dbus/system_bus_socket ]; then
+			break
+		fi
+		sleep 1
+	done
 	start-stop-daemon --start --background $SSD_OPTIONS
 	echo "${DAEMON##*/}."
   ;;
